1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,030
Welcome to the Fiddy Working Heritage Farm.

2
00:00:05,030 --> 00:00:11,330
This open-air museum gives you the experience of agriculture and rural life in the

3
00:00:11,330 --> 00:00:14,600
English countryside at the end of the nineteenth century.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:18,153
So you'll see a typical farm of that period,

5
00:00:18,153 --> 00:00:22,650
and like me, all the staff are dressed in clothes of that time.

6
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:28,210
I must give you some advice and safety tips before we go any further.

7
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:33,650
As it's a working farm, please don't frighten or injure the animals.

8
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:35,182
We have a lot here,

9
00:00:35,182 --> 00:00:38,750
and many of them are breeds that are now quite rare.

10
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:43,160
And do stay at a safe distance from the tools:

11
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:47,421
some of them have sharp points which can be pretty dangerous,

12
00:00:47,421 --> 00:00:49,330
so please don't touch them.

13
00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:51,610
We don't want any accidents, do we?

14
00:00:51,610 --> 00:00:54,783
The ground is very uneven,

15
00:00:54,783 --> 00:01:00,045
and you might slip if you're wearing sandals so l'm glad to see you're

16
00:01:00,045 --> 00:01:01,290
all wearing shoes

17
00:01:01,290 --> 00:01:04,050
we always advise people to do that.

18
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:08,340
Now, children of all ages are very welcome here,

19
00:01:08,340 --> 00:01:13,278
and usually even very young children love the ducks and lambs,

20
00:01:13,278 --> 00:01:16,490
so do bring them along next time you come.

21
00:01:16,490 --> 00:01:20,832
I don't think any of you have brought dogs with you,

22
00:01:20,832 --> 00:01:22,440
but in case you have,

23
00:01:22,440 --> 00:01:27,510
l'm afraid they'll have to stay in the car park, unless they're guide dogs.

24
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:32,767
I'm sure you'll understand that they could cause a lot of problems on a

25
00:01:32,767 --> 00:01:33,130
farm.

26
00:01:33,130 --> 00:01:42,040
Now let me give you some idea of the layout of the farm.

27
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:47,598
The building where you bought your tickets is the New Barn, immediately to your

28
00:01:47,598 --> 00:01:47,900
right,

29
00:01:47,900 --> 00:01:52,243
and we're now at the beginning of the main path to the farmland -

30
00:01:52,243 --> 00:01:55,600
and of course the car park is on your left.

31
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:00,867
The scarecrow you can see in the car park in the corner beside the

32
00:02:00,867 --> 00:02:01,550
main path,

33
00:02:01,550 --> 00:02:06,112
is a traditional figure for keeping the birds away from crops,

34
00:02:06,112 --> 00:02:09,710
but our scarecrow is a permanent sculpture.

35
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:12,284
It's taller than a human being,

36
00:02:12,284 --> 00:02:15,200
so you can see it from quite a distance.

37
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:19,650
If you look ahead of you, you'll see a maze.

38
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:25,434
It's opposite the New Barn, beside the side path that branches off to the

39
00:02:25,434 --> 00:02:26,900
right just over there.

40
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:32,946
The maze is made out of hedges which are too tall for young children

41
00:02:32,946 --> 00:02:33,890
to see over them,

42
00:02:33,890 --> 00:02:35,544
but it's quite small,

43
00:02:35,544 --> 00:02:37,400
so you can't get lost in it!

44
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:43,457
Now, can you see the bridge crossing the fish pool further up the main

45
00:02:43,457 --> 00:02:43,900
path?

46
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:48,540
If you want to go to the cafe, go towards the bridge

47
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:50,850
and turn right just before it.

48
00:02:50,850 --> 00:02:56,528
Walk along the side path and the cafe's on the first bend you come

49
00:02:56,528 --> 00:02:56,750
to.

50
00:02:56,750 --> 00:03:00,413
The building was originally the schoolhouse,

51
00:03:00,413 --> 00:03:03,230
and it's well over a hundred years old.

52
00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:12,256
As you may know, we run skills workshops here, where you can learn traditional crafts like woodwork

53
00:03:12,256 --> 00:03:13,580
and basket-making.

54
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:16,939
You can see examples of the work,

55
00:03:16,939 --> 00:03:20,740
and talk to someone about the courses, in the Black Bam.

56
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:26,248
If you take the side path to the right, here, just by the New

57
00:03:26,248 --> 00:03:26,650
Barn,

58
00:03:26,650 --> 00:03:31,060
you'll come to the Black Barn just where the path first bends.

59
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:37,223
Now I mustn't forget to tell you about picnicking, as I can see some

60
00:03:37,223 --> 00:03:39,150
of you have brought your lunch with you.

61
00:03:39,150 --> 00:03:44,720
You can picnic in the field, though do clear up behind you, of course.

62
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:50,382
Or if you'd prefer a covered picnic area, there's one near the farmyard:

63
00:03:50,382 --> 00:03:52,450
just after you cross the bridge,

64
00:03:52,450 --> 00:03:55,400
there's a covered picnic spot on the right.

65
00:03:55,400 --> 00:04:00,370
And the last thing to mention is Fiddy House itself.

66
00:04:00,370 --> 00:04:05,932
From here you can cross the bridge then walk along the footpath through the

67
00:04:05,932 --> 00:04:08,040
field to the left of the farmyard.

68
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,197
That goes to the house,

69
00:04:10,197 --> 00:04:13,060
and it'll give you a lovely view of it.

70
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:16,052
It's certainly worth a few photographs,

71
00:04:16,052 --> 00:04:20,630
but as it's a private home, I'm afraid you can't go inside.

72
00:04:20,630 --> 00:04:22,038
Right.

73
00:04:22,038 --> 00:04:27,270
Well, if you're all ready, well set off on our tour of the farm.
